    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so if i go buy a bag with a higher middle number, will that fix the purple patches fairly quickly? also is there anything else i should check for in the soil to make sure the phosphorus is actually being absorbed properly? i don't want to just throw money away if there's something else blocking it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While a higher middle number fertilizer is a good starting point, you shouldn't expect a quick fix, as plants take time to process nutrients, especially when the soil is already stressed. It's a much more thorough process than just tossing a bag of fertilizer down, which is what some of those low-level, quick-fix green-up products do. You need to get a proper soil test, which is the only way to know definitively if the phosphorus is *there* but *unavailable* to your fescue. This test will tell you about pH levels and organic matter, which are critical factors in phosphorus absorption.",
